# roughness_knobs.mac — THE roughness settings of the pTP film, in one place.
#
# Applied in full by every macro (run.mac, run_vuv_spectrum.mac, run_285.mac,
# draw_offscreen.mac) when the simulation is started with rough=on (main.sh:
# ROUGH=on, which defines the macro alias {ROUGH} = 1), and always by
# vis_roughness.mac. With rough=off nothing here is applied and the film stays
# exactly as configured in the YAML (pTPlayerThickness_mm, pTPsigmaAlpha_rad,
# pTPgeomRough*). Edit the values below, nothing else.
#
# Film thickness [mm]
/detector/pTPlayerthickness 1.0
#
# Surface variation: random Gaussian height map on the beam-facing face of the
# film (tessellated solid; the acrylic-facing face stays flat).
#   bumps per side: lateral bump size = film side / cells (150 mm / 30 = 5 mm);
#   0 = flat film
/detector/pTPgeomRoughCells 30
#   RMS bump height [mm]; clipped at ±3 RMS and at 0.8 × film thickness
/detector/pTPgeomRoughAmp 0.3
#   seed of the height map (same seed = same surface in every run)
/detector/pTPgeomRoughSeed 12345
#
# Optional statistical micro-facet slope of the pTP faces [rad] (Geant4
# UNIFIED model), added on top of the geometric surface variation above.
# 0 = off: the roughness of the run is the height map alone.
/detector/pTPsigmaAlpha 0.0
#
/run/reinitializeGeometry
/run/initialize
